{
  "spec": "aadistill.artifact_spec/v1",
  "session": "autoinit_c1",
  "note": "Success spec for a Phase-C1 run that reached ALL_DONE. It implements the frozen evidence_manifest_contract of logs/phase_c1_execution_preregistration.json, entry by entry. Two path facts decide every pattern here and neither is guessable. (1) C1Driver subclasses PhaseADriver, so it inherits that module's AUDIT = artifacts/audit/autoinit_phase_a, its probe out_dir artifacts/stage3/phase_a/<probe_id>, and its generation dir artifacts/eval/phase_a/<probe_id>. The C1 records land there too, NOT under audit/autoinit_c1 -- the launcher's ArtifactPolicy.audit_dirname only decides where session_runner copies the run log and where it scp's report_names. Both roots therefore appear below. (2) Every per-probe class is pinned to the probe_id prefix autoinit.v1.phase_c1. so a stale Phase-A or Phase-B artifact left in the same tree cannot satisfy a C1 minimum. Counts: 6 probes = 2 arms x 3 seeds; 42 = 6 probes x the 7 sets of c1_confirmation_v1 (gsm8k, math_verified, multihop, rag, knowledge, tool, code), because uncapped_eval writes one <set>.generations.jsonl and one <set>.json per set. Requiring 6 here rather than 42 would accept a probe that generated one set out of seven. Entries are ArtifactSpec kwargs; the manifest root is artifacts/.",
  "entries": [
    {
